 "caption": "Someone painted over a god in this Vermeer.\n\nVermeer painted Girl Reading a Letter at an Open Window in Delft around 1657–59. On the wall behind her hung a painting of Cupid. Decades after Vermeer died in 1675, someone covered Cupid with paint and left a blank wall. Nobody knows who, or why.\n\nAn X-ray found him in 1979, and for decades experts assumed Vermeer had changed his mind and hidden Cupid himself. Then in 2017 Dresden's restorers looked closer: under the cover-up, on top of Cupid's varnish, was a layer of dirt. Cupid had hung there in plain sight for decades. It wasn't Vermeer.\n\nBy 2021 the overpaint was gone. Cupid is back, stepping on a mask, a symbol of love without deceit. Experts think she's reading a love letter.\n\nP.S. The same Cupid hangs on the wall in another Vermeer: A Young Woman Standing at a Virginal, in London's National Gallery.\n\n🖤 Which version do you prefer: with Cupid or without?",
 "caption_short": "Someone painted over a god in this Vermeer, and for decades experts blamed Vermeer himself. A layer of dirt proved them wrong. 🖤",
 "youtube_title": "Who hid on this wall for 200 years? Vermeer's hidden Cupid",
